<div class="nav-bar"><a class="nav-link" href="pt_01_UP_向上、完结体、视线显露与靠近.html" title="01_UP_向上、完结体、视线显露与靠近">01 UP <span class="nav-cnt">(645)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_02_OUT_观察者三视角(消失_显露_丧失)与延展.html" title="02_OUT_观察者三视角(消失/显露/丧失)与延展">02 OUT <span class="nav-cnt">(576)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_03_OFF_脱离支撑表面、取消切断、起飞引爆与完结.html" title="03_OFF_脱离支撑表面、取消切断、起飞引爆与完结">03 OFF <span class="nav-cnt">(305)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_04_DOWN_向下、数值减弱、压制瓦解与落笔记录.html" title="04_DOWN_向下、数值减弱、压制瓦解与落笔记录">04 DOWN <span class="nav-cnt">(243)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_05_IN_功能性包容、状态容器、吸收与向内坍塌.html" title="05_IN_功能性包容、状态容器、吸收与向内坍塌">05 IN <span class="nav-cnt">(246)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_06_ON_前行延续(ON²)vs表面支撑_基础_负担(ON¹).html" title="06_ON_前行延续(ON²) vs 表面支撑/基础/负担(ON¹)">06 ON <span class="nav-cnt">(178)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_07_OVER_弧线跨越、全面审视、翻转倒下与移交克服.html" title="07_OVER_弧线跨越、全面审视、翻转倒下与移交克服">07 OVER <span class="nav-cnt">(133)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_08_AWAY_远离分离、彻底处置、渐进消逝与持续劳作.html" title="08_AWAY_远离分离、彻底处置、渐进消逝与持续劳作">08 AWAY <span class="nav-cnt">(114)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_09_BACK_回到起点、对等回击、向后退缩与抑制隐瞒.html" title="09_BACK_回到起点、对等回击、向后退缩与抑制隐瞒">09 BACK <span class="nav-cnt">(101)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_10_THROUGH_穿过三维通道、熬过难关与彻底审阅.html" title="10_THROUGH_穿过三维通道、熬过难关与彻底审阅">10 THROUGH <span class="nav-cnt">(47)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_11_AROUND_环绕旋转、漫无目的闲逛、规避与苏醒.html" title="11_AROUND_环绕旋转、漫无目的闲逛、规避与苏醒">11 AROUND <span class="nav-cnt">(72)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_12_INTO_动态穿越边界、猛烈碰撞、深入调查与形态转化.html" title="12_INTO_动态穿越边界、猛烈碰撞、深入调查与形态转化">12 INTO <span class="nav-cnt">(41)</span></a><a class="nav-link active" href="pt_13_其他常见小品词.html" title="13_其他常见小品词">13 其他小品词 <span class="nav-cnt">(365)</span></a></div>
<div class='page-hero'><div><h1 class='hero-title'>13 · 其他常见小品词</h1><p class='hero-sub'>FOR / WITH / BY / AFTER / APART / ASIDE — EPE Ch.5, 11, 18, 19</p></div><div style='font-size:0.88em;color:#475569;font-weight:600;'>共 <b>365</b> 个独立义项 • <b>1095</b> 句中英对照例句</div></div>
<details class='epe-book-drawer' open><summary class='epe-drawer-bar'><span>📚 《English Prepositions Explained》(Seth Lindstromberg) 原著核心精讲 — Chapter 2 (TO, FROM), Chapter 5 (ALONG, ASIDE, AGAINST), Chapter 9 (ACROSS), Chapter 11 (BY), Chapter 18 (WITH, APART), Chapter 19 (FOR)</span><span style='font-size:0.84em;color:#6366f1;font-weight:600;'>点击收起 / 展开原书理论图式 ▾</span></summary><div class='epe-drawer-grid'><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>🧭 原著空间与功能核心图式 (Core Schema)</div><div><b>水平伴随、旁侧分离、十字横跨与源头/目标导向</b>：本页汇集了 EPE 其余核心章节的小品词图式——包括 <b>ALONG</b>（顺长轴无阻力巡航与并肩同行 Fig.5.9）、<b>ASIDE</b>（拨向视线或前进路线左右两侧）、<b>ACROSS</b>（十字垂直横跨沟壑 Fig.9.16）、<b>FROM</b>（离开起点与阻止 `NOT →`）、<b>BY/PAST</b>（擦身掠过或近旁待命）以及 <b>WITH/FOR/TO</b>。</div><div class='epe-box-title' style='margin-top:12px;'>📝 原书典型语料例句 (Authentic Examples from EPE)</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>Several times he waved bodyguards aside... / set aside their differences / put time aside for book reading.</i> [Ch.5 (11), (14), (19)]</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>It's critical that you learn how to get your point across... / I came across a question in a forum.</i> [Ch.9 (46)-(47)]</div></div><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>⚖️ 原书近义小品词深度辨析与隐喻机制 (Key Contrasts & Metaphors)</div><ul class='epe-contrast-list'><li><b>ALONG (Ch.5 §2.1 & §3.1 Fig.5.9)</b>：源于 <i>on² + long</i>，自带“顺畅巡航（effortless cruising）”色彩；在 <i>get along / go along with</i> 中，把两人关系描绘为两条并排顺畅延伸、既不冲突也不分道扬镳的生命轨迹。</li><li><b>ASIDE (Ch.5 §4)</b>：将障碍物或私密对象移到主视线/前进路线（Line of sight/advance）的左或右侧——用于忽略排斥时带负面色彩（<i>brush/sweep/shunt aside</i>），用于留存资源时呈正面色彩（<i>set/put time or money aside</i>）。</li><li><b>ACROSS (Ch.7 & Ch.9 §5.4)</b>：含 <i>cross</i>（十字交叉），在 <i>get your point across</i> 中隐含参照物是“沟通鸿沟（the communication gap）”，在 <i>come across</i> 中源于十字路口两条路径的偶然相交（<i>cross sb's path</i>）。</li><li><b>FROM 的阻止逻辑 (Ch.2 §9.2.3)</b>：为什么 <i>keep/stop A from doing B</i> 表阻止？因为 `TO` 是走向目标（`→ B`），而作为反义词的 `FROM` 在此等于 `NOT → B`！</li></ul></div></div></details>

